IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P8-gate`

-- P8-art73: Article 73, reporting of serious incidents (Chapter IX Section 2). LAYER 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Group General (from 2 August 2026; Art 111(2) can save a high-risk AI system placed on the market earlier).
-- The Omnibus did not change Article 73 itself; Article 75(1a) (P8-art75) derogates from it for the AI Office's systems.
-- Seam S10: whether an event is a "serious incident" comes from Art 3(49) (aia-definitions.l4); here it is a BOOLEAN input named for it.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 73 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 73(1) report the serious incident to the market surveillance authorities of the Member States where the incident occurred`
    `Art 73(5) submit an initial report that is incomplete, followed by a complete report`
    `Art 73(6) perform the necessary investigations in relation to the serious incident and the AI system concerned`
    `Art 73(6) cooperate with the competent authorities and, where relevant, the notified body concerned`
    `Art 73(6) perform an investigation which involves altering the AI system concerned in a way which may affect any subsequent evaluation of the causes of the incident`
    `Art 73(7) inform the national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1)`
    `Art 73(7) develop and issue dedicated guidance to facilitate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1`
    `Art 73(7) assess the guidance regularly`
    `Art 73(8) take appropriate measures as provided for in Article 19 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020`
    `Art 73(8) follow the notification procedures provided in Regulation (EU) 2019/1020`
    `Art 73(11) notify the Commission of the serious incident`

§ `Article 73(1): the duty to report`

-- src:1130 | 1. Providers of high-risk AI systems placed on the Union market shall report any serious incident to the market surveillance authorities of the Member States where that incident occurred.
@ref Art 73(1) (src:1130)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is placed on the Union market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event is a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 73(1) the provider must report the serious incident to the market surveillance authorities of the Member States where the incident occurred` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 73 1
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the AI system is a high-risk AI system` `the route to high-risk`)
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision speaks of high-risk AI systems
              ELSE IF NOT `the AI system is placed on the Union market`
                   THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "high-risk AI systems placed on the Union market" is a scope limit with no "only" (ruling (c))
                   ELSE IF NOT `the event is a serious incident`
                        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to report "any serious incident"; Art 3(49) says what one is
                        ELSE IF `the AI system is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to Article 75(1)`
                             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "By way of derogation from Article 73, providers of high-risk AI systems subject to the competence of the AI Office ... shall report any serious incidents to the AI Office" (Art 75(1a), as amended)
                             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1130 | 1. Providers of high-risk AI systems placed on the Union market shall report any serious incident to the market surveillance authorities of the Member States where that incident occurred.
@ref Art 73(1) (src:1130)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is placed on the Union market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event is a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to Article 75(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report has been made to the market surveillance authority of each Member State where the incident occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 73(1) the provider has reported the serious incident to the market surveillance authority of each Member State where the incident occurred` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 73 1
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE CONSIDER `Art 73(1) the provider must report the serious incident to the market surveillance authorities of the Member States where the incident occurred` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the AI system is placed on the Union market` `the event is a serious incident` `the AI system is subject to the competence of the AI Office pursuant to Article 75(1)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the report has been made to the market surveillance authority of each Member State where the incident occurred`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall report any serious incident to the market surveillance authorities of the Member States where that incident occurred" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no duty to report to the market surveillance authorities arises on these facts (see the function above)

§ `Article 73(2) to (4): the time limits`

-- Paragraph 2: "not later than 15 days after the provider or, where applicable, the deployer, becomes aware". The input is the date of that awareness.
-- src:1131 | 2. The report referred to in paragraph 1 shall be made immediately after the provider has established a causal link between the AI system and the serious incident or the reasonable likelihood of such a link, and, in any event, not later than 15 days after the provider or, where applicable, the deployer, becomes aware of the serious incident.
@ref Art 73(2) first subparagraph (src:1131)
