             JUST (`the lesser of` (`Art 73(2) to (4) the days that the paragraph gives or else the fallback` (`Art 73(3) the number of days after becoming aware within which the report must be provided` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the event is a widespread infringement` `the event is a serious incident as defined in Article 3, point (49)(b)`) `the days under paragraph 2`) (`Art 73(2) to (4) the days that the paragraph gives or else the fallback` (`Art 73(4) the number of days after becoming aware within which the report must be provided` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the event is the death of a person`) `the days under paragraph 2`))
             WHERE
                 GIVEN `the first` IS A NUMBER
                       `the second` IS A NUMBER
                 GIVETH A NUMBER
                 `the lesser of` MEANS IF `the first` AT MOST `the second` THEN `the first` ELSE `the second`

-- "shall be made immediately after the provider has established a causal link ..., and, in any event, not later than 15 days after the provider or, where applicable,
-- the deployer, becomes aware" (paragraph 2); "immediately, and not later than two days" (paragraph 3); "immediately after ... but not later than 10 days" (paragraph 4).
-- "Immediately" is a judgment the text leaves open (an input); the outer limit is a period the text fixes in its own words (ruling (a): outside it, JUST FALSE).
