-- The bar: "shall not perform any investigation which involves altering the AI system concerned in a way which may affect any subsequent evaluation
-- of the causes of the incident, prior to informing the competent authorities of such action". A flat negative with an end the text names (N2 and the "until" ruling (d)): JUST TRUE until the competent authorities are informed, JUST FALSE once they are, NOTHING where the investigation involves no alteration that may affect the later evaluation (fork F-73-6-until).
-- src:1137 | The provider shall cooperate with the competent authorities, and where relevant with the notified body concerned, during the investigations referred to in the first subparagraph, and shall not perform any investigation which involves altering the AI system concerned in a way which may affect any subsequent evaluation of the causes of the incident, prior to informing the competent authorities of such action.
@ref Art 73(6) second subparagraph (src:1137)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the investigation involves altering the AI system concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration may affect any subsequent evaluation of the causes of the incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authorities have been informed of the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 73(6) second subparagraph the provider is barred from performing the investigation that alters the AI system before informing the competent authorities` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 73 6
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the AI system is a high-risk AI system` `the route to high-risk`)
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision speaks of high-risk AI systems
              ELSE IF `the investigation involves altering the AI system concerned` AND `the alteration may affect any subsequent evaluation of the causes of the incident`
                   THEN IF (NOT `the competent authorities have been informed of the action`)
                        THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not perform any investigation which involves altering the AI system concerned in a way which may affect any subsequent evaluation of the causes of the incident, prior to informing the competent authorities" (a flat negative: the bar holds until the authorities are informed)
                        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an "until" bar, ruling (d) of 2026-11-05 ("Delegated definitions, defences and "until" bars"): "prior to informing the competent authorities" is the event X, so the bar is `JUST TRUE` before X and `JUST FALSE` after X (fork F-73-6-until)
                   ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is limited to an alteration that may affect the later evaluation, a scope limit with no "only" (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05)

-- The same two duties as regulative rules. The investigation and the cooperation carry no time limit ("without delay") and no consequence; the prohibition is a SHANT
-- that holds until the competent authorities are informed (an input, counted in days from the start), so a trace in which the forbidden act occurs reaches BREACH.
