§ `Article 73(7): the market surveillance authority informs, and the Commission's guidance`

-- src:1138 | 7. Upon receiving a notification related to a serious incident referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c), the relevant market surveillance authority shall inform the national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1). The Commission shall develop dedicated guidance to facilitate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1 of this Article. That guidance shall be issued by 2 August 2025, and shall be assessed regularly.
@ref Art 73(7) first sentence (src:1138)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the market surveillance authority has received a notification related to a serious incident referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 73(7) first sentence the market surveillance authority must inform the national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1)` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the market surveillance authority has received a notification related to a serious incident referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon receiving a notification related to a serious incident referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c)" (an unmet "upon" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (c) of 2026-11-05) (fork F-73-7-first-duty)

