§ `Article 73(9) and (10): equivalent reporting regimes and medical devices`

-- src:1140 | 9. For high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III that are placed on the market or put into service by providers that are subject to Union legislative instruments laying down reporting obligations equivalent to those set out in this Regulation, the notification of serious incidents shall be limited to those referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c).
@ref Art 73(9) (src:1140)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is a high-risk AI system referred to in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is placed on the market or put into service by a provider subject to Union legislative instruments laying down reporting obligations equivalent to those set out in this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the serious incident is one referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 73(9) the provider's notification of the serious incident is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 73 9
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF (NOT `the AI system is a high-risk AI system referred to in Annex III`) OR (NOT `the AI system is placed on the market or put into service by a provider subject to Union legislative instruments laying down reporting obligations equivalent to those set out in this Regulation`)
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 9 is for "high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III" placed by providers "subject to Union legislative instruments laying down reporting obligations equivalent to those" of this Regulation (a scope limit with no "only", ruling (c))
              ELSE IF `the serious incident is one referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c)`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notification of serious incidents shall be limited to those referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c)"

-- src:1141 | 10. For high-risk AI systems which are safety components of devices, or are themselves devices, covered by Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746, the notification of serious incidents shall be limited to those referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c) of this Regulation, and shall be made to the national competent authority chosen for that purpose by the Member States where the incident occurred.
@ref Art 73(10) (src:1141)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is a safety component of a device, or is itself a device, covered by Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the serious incident is one referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 73(10) the notification of the serious incident is within the limit for a device` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 73 10
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF NOT `the AI system is a safety component of a device, or is itself a device, covered by Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 10 is for "high-risk AI systems which are safety components of devices, or are themselves devices, covered by Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746" (a scope limit with no "only", ruling (c))
              ELSE IF `the serious incident is one referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c)`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notification of serious incidents shall be limited to those referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c)"

-- src:1141 | 10. For high-risk AI systems which are safety components of devices, or are themselves devices, covered by Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746, the notification of serious incidents shall be limited to those referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c) of this Regulation, and shall be made to the national competent authority chosen for that purpose by the Member States where the incident occurred.
@ref Art 73(10) (src:1141)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is a safety component of a device, or is itself a device, covered by Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority notified is the national competent authority chosen for that purpose by the Member State where the incident occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 73(10) the notification is made to the national competent authority chosen for that purpose` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 73 10
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF NOT `the AI system is a safety component of a device, or is itself a device, covered by Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 10 is for devices covered by Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746
              ELSE JUST `the authority notified is the national competent authority chosen for that purpose by the Member State where the incident occurred`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be made to the national competent authority chosen for that purpose by the Member States where the incident occurred" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

§ `Article 73(11): national competent authorities notify the Commission`

-- src:1142 | 11. National competent authorities shall immediately notify the Commission of any serious incident, whether or not they have taken action on it, in accordance with Article 20 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020.
@ref Art 73(11) (src:1142)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the national competent authority has been notified of a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the national competent authority has taken action on the serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 73(11) the national competent authority must notify the Commission of the serious incident` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the national competent authority has been notified of a serious incident`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- "of any serious incident, whether or not they have taken action on it": the answer does not turn on whether action was taken
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to notify "any serious incident" the authority knows of; the text is silent on one it has not been notified of

-- src:1142 | 11. National competent authorities shall immediately notify the Commission of any serious incident, whether or not they have taken action on it, in accordance with Article 20 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020.
@ref Art 73(11) (src:1142)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the national competent authority has been notified of a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 73 act`
`Art 73(11) the national competent authority's duty to notify the Commission immediately` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the national competent authority has been notified of a serious incident`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group does not apply on the date asked, or no serious incident is known to the authority
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party national competent authority`
        MUST `Art 73(11) notify the Commission of the serious incident`
        HENCE FULFILLED
